  <prompt>Author toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts at src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts with modal-size constants (Layout 1 = 85%x85% for sprk_recordsummary/SmartTodo; Notepad = 70%x80%) and target=2 (modal). Constants become the single source of truth for modal sizing across all toolbar-action-hook consumers.</prompt>

  <role>Spaarke platform developer. Familiar with Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo modal options.</role>

  <goal>toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts present with typed constants exported; used by 012 and 030+.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §3.4 identifies these size constants. Layout 1 = 85%x85% comes from R2 modal standard (docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md). Notepad's 70%x80% is a specialized-editor sizing.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Notepad launch contract: 70%x80% modal (specialized editor sizing per FR-10).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">SmartTodo launch: Layout 1 (85%x85%) per FR-09.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">These constants MUST match docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md Layout 1 dimensions.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/record-modal-selection.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    <existing>Modal size constants are scattered across R2 project code (SmartTodo, etc.) as inline literals.</existing>
    <extension>No shared constants module exists.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Modal sizing drifts across consumers when R3 introduces a new size or R2 revises Layout 1 dimensions.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Author toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts exporting: LAYOUT_1_MODAL = { target: 2, position: 1, width: {value: 85, unit: "%"}, height: {value: 85, unit: "%"} }; NOTEPAD_MODAL = { target: 2, position: 1, width: {value: 70, unit: "%"}, height: {value: 80, unit: "%"} }.</step>
    <step order="2">Also export NOTEPAD_WEBRESOURCE_NAME = "sprk_notepad_page"; SMARTTODO_WEBRESOURCE_NAME = "sprk_smarttodo_page"; RECORDSUMMARY_FIELD = "sprk_recordsummary" (per task 001 correction — this is a MULTILINE TEXT field on the record, NOT an entity name).</step>
    <step order="2.1">Also export SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS = { sprk_matter: "sprk_regardingmatter", sprk_project: "sprk_regardingproject", sprk_event: "sprk_regardingevent", sprk_invoice: "sprk_regardinginvoice", sprk_budget: "sprk_regardingbudget", sprk_workassignment: "sprk_regardingworkassignment" } — the 6 entity-specific-lookup mappings from ADR-024 dual-field pattern.</step>
    <step order="3">Add TypeScript types for the constants (or import from Xrm typings if available in the shared lib).</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 011 ✅.</step>
    <step order="5">Document deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools><tool name="npm">Build</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">File exists with named exports LAYOUT_1_MODAL, NOTEPAD_MODAL, NOTEPAD_WEBRESOURCE_NAME, SMARTTODO_WEBRESOURCE_NAME, RECORDSUMMARY_FIELD, SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Values match spec dimensions exactly.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>SMARTTODO_WEBRESOURCE_NAME must be verified against target environment in task 020 (may need adjustment).</notes>

